  "body": "Found while working #1057 (on a full-fidelity model, so not a fidelity bug).\n\n**What happens.** A Thread (thread mill) operation sourced from a model is convicted with `Gouge` on every helix move, and `Crossing` pairs, even at full fidelity. Fixture: `crates/app/tests/coarse_rims.rs` on `issue/1057-drill-excess-false-gouge` (PR for #1057) - the 40 x 40 x 20 block with a 20 x 20 cavity blind at Z 10, a 6 mm Tap-form thread mill (pitch 1), one `Hole { xy: (0,0), radius: 5.0, floor_z: 10.2 }`, `SrcRef::Entity(\"part\")`: blocking warnings `Gouge { at: 4..=55 }` plus `Crossing { moves: [3, 56] } ...`.\n\n**Likely cause.** The Thread kind verifies `Mode::Boundary` against the drill's rim region (`material_source::source_region`, Bore/Thread arm), and law (b) reads the declared rim at `r - tol`. A thread mill's helix runs the thread depth H (0.5413 x pitch) PAST the declared circle by design (`mill2d_c::thread_helices_are_timed_by_the_tools_pitch`: rho up to R + H - r), so every helix point reads as a gouge of about H against the rim. `mill2d_c` sources its threads from the stock, so it never sees this.\n\n**What is owed.** Decide what a thread mill's rim is (the declared minor circle grown by the thread depth, or the major diameter) so a matched thread mill verifies clean against a model, while one cutting past the thread's major diameter still convicts; and look at the `Crossing` pairs on the same path.\n\n**Done means:** a matched thread mill on a model-sourced hole verifies clean at full fidelity and near the refusal bound (`coarse_rims::a_thread_mill_reads_the_same_near_the_bound_as_at_full_fidelity` then tightens to `== Vec::new()`), and an oversize thread still convicts.\n",
